## Context

`tickets/tools/go/main.go` is currently 1305 lines in a single file.
Most subcommands now exist (`validate`, `ready`, `archive`, `graph`,
`next-id`, `close`, `version`, `update`). The 0008 (`erg pick`) work
will add another command and tip the file past a comfortable size.
Splitting now, before pick lands, gives that work a natural home.

This ticket inherits the modularization + godoc portion of 0006.
The other portions of 0006 are gone: `close` shipped in PR #7;
`claim`/`release` are dropped per 0013.

## Actions

### A. Split `main.go`

Proposed boundaries (refine during implementation):

- `ticket.go` — `Erg` struct, `parseErg`, `loadTickets`, header
  validation, log-line validation, `findTicketFile(id)`,
  `appendToTicket`, the `statusLineRE` and other shared regexps.
- `validate.go` — `cmdValidate` and helpers used only by it.
- `ready.go` — `cmdReady` and its plaintext/JSON formatters.
- `archive.go` — `cmdArchive` and date-resolution helpers.
- `graph.go` — `cmdGraph`, `annotate()`, DAG construction.
- `nextid.go` — `cmdNextID`.
- `close.go` — `cmdClose`.
- `selfupdate.go` — `cmdVersion`, `cmdUpdate`, `selfHash`, the
  `updateURL` constant.
- `main.go` — `main()`, `printUsage()`, command dispatch only.

Each file under ~500 lines. Each gets a package-level godoc comment
on its first declaration. Each exported or key unexported function
gets a one-line godoc starting with its name (`// cmdReady prints
…`).

### B. godoc audit

- `go doc ./tickets/tools/go/...` produces clean, complete output.
- `printUsage()` remains the single source of truth for CLI help.

### C. Tests

- `go test ./tickets/tools/go/...` and `make test` green after each
  commit (split file-by-file rather than in one large move).
- No behavior change. `make validate` green on `tickets/`.

## Open question — CLI shape

0006 raised a `gh`-style noun-first redesign:
`erg ticket list/validate/close/...` instead of `erg ready/validate/close`.
The case for it is muscle-memory parity with `gh`; the case against
is a breaking rename of an interface that just shipped two new verbs
(`close` in #7, `version`/`update` in #5).

**Recommendation: defer.** Keep verb-first for now; revisit once the
modularization is in and the file structure makes a future rename a
mechanical change. If revisited, file as a separate ticket.

## Out of scope

- Any new subcommand (pick, claim, release, etc.).
- CLI rename to noun-first form (deferred — see above).
- Test coverage expansion beyond keeping existing tests green.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] `main.go` split per §A; each file under ~500 lines
- [ ] `go doc ./tickets/tools/go/...` produces clean output for every
      exported declaration
- [ ] `go test ./tickets/tools/go/...` green
- [ ] `make test` and `make validate` green
- [ ] No `printUsage()` text changes (interface unchanged)
